## 1. Overview

### 1.1 Purpose
Khan Institute requires a 4-page informational and lead-generation website to establish an online presence, showcase available courses, display institute photos, and allow prospective students to submit course applications/inquiries directly through the site.

### 1.2 Background
The client (an educational/vocational training institute offering courses like Computer, Abacus, Tailoring, Beautician, Spoken English, etc.) has provided a hand-drawn wireframe specifying site structure, navigation, and required content sections.

### 1.3 Goals
- Establish a professional online presence for Khan Institute
- Enable prospective students to browse courses and apply online
- Showcase institute photos/facilities via a gallery
- Provide easy access to contact information and office location
- Capture lead data (name, father's name, course, mobile) for admissions follow-up

### 1.4 Success Metrics
- Number of application form submissions per month
- Website visits / unique users
- Bounce rate on Courses page
- Contact page engagement (clicks on phone numbers)
- Mobile vs desktop traffic split (site must work well on both)

