## 6. Data & Backend Requirements

### 6.1 Application Submissions — via WhatsApp (No API)
- **Mechanism:** Uses WhatsApp's free **"click-to-chat" link** (`https://wa.me/<number>?text=<prefilled-message>`) — **not** the paid WhatsApp Business API. No backend server, database, or third-party account required.
- **Flow:**
  1. Student fills the form (Student's Name, Father's Name, Course, Mobile Number)
  2. JavaScript validates the fields and builds a formatted text message from the entered data
  3. On clicking "Apply" / "Submit," JavaScript opens WhatsApp (app on mobile, WhatsApp Web on desktop) with the institute's number and the message **pre-filled**
  4. Student taps **Send** inside WhatsApp to actually deliver the inquiry — this final tap is required by WhatsApp's own click-to-chat design and cannot be automated
- **Which number receives it:** To be confirmed by client — e.g., Development Manager (7501288478) or Managing Director (8926789705), or a dedicated admissions WhatsApp number
- **Limitations to flag to client:**
  - Requires the student's device to have WhatsApp installed (or WhatsApp Web on desktop)
  - The message is only sent once the student manually taps Send inside WhatsApp — Claude/the website cannot force-send it
  - No stored database of leads on the website itself; all records live in the institute's WhatsApp chat history
  - If a searchable/exportable lead list is wanted later, an optional low-cost addition (e.g., logging a copy to a simple Google Sheet in parallel) can be discussed — out of scope for v1 unless requested

### 6.2 Content Management
- Confirmed: course list, gallery images, and page content will be **static/hardcoded** in the HTML files. The developer updates content (new courses, new photos) when the client requests changes — no admin panel or CMS in v1.

